Begin from the noninteracting limit $U=0$ and the Bloch Hamiltonian in momentum space under periodic boundary conditions: define crystal momentum $k$, the phase functions $\varphi_\pm(k)=\phi/2\pm k$, and the two-by-two Bloch Hamiltonian
$H(k)=\begin{bmatrix}
J_R^a e^{i\varphi_+}+J_L^a e^{-i\varphi_+} & K\\[4pt]
K & J_R^b e^{-i\varphi_-}+J_L^b e^{i\varphi_-}
\end{bmatrix},$
whose two complex band energies are denoted $E_n(k)$ for band index $n=1,2$. This Bloch Hamiltonian is the starting point for spectral-topology analysis of the non-Hermitian system.

Since the columns of V and W form an orthonormal set, they can be extended to an orthonormal basis of C^n. We define coefficients of Psi_n in this basis:
alpha_n = V^dagger Psi_n,  beta_n = W^dagger Psi_n
Substituting the SVD into the recursion and multiplying by V^dagger and W^dagger yields:
alpha_n = G_vv Xi beta_{n+1} + G_wv Xi alpha_{n-1}
beta_n = G_vw Xi beta_{n+1} + G_ww Xi alpha_{n-1}
where we define G_{AB} = B^dagger G A for A,B in {V,W}.

Diagonalize $H_{\mathrm{eff}}$ (i.e., solve the eigenproblem $(H_{\mathrm{eff}}-E)\Psi=0$) to obtain four complex eigenvalues labeled $E_{e_{
u}}$ and $E_{h_{
u}}$ ($
u=1,2$), given compactly by
$E_{e_{
u}(h_{
u})}=-i \Gamma \pm \sqrt{A_{1}(k)+(-1)^{
u} 2 \sqrt{A_{2}(k)}}$,
where the $\pm$ corresponds to the two branches within each electron-like or hole-like pair and the label $
u=1(2)$ denotes the first (second) member of each pair. This formula follows directly from substituting the explicit matrix forms of $H_{\mathrm{closed}}^{1\mathrm{D}}$ and $\Sigma^{r}$ into $H_{\mathrm{eff}}$ and computing its eigenvalues. [47]
